From 3f88c82cb8b7cbfc515ab89c3434125bd5b8eaab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 13:27:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep a CSS escape from ending a rule, and drop three invalid
 declarations

Four error-recovery bugs, each of which Acid2's parser section exercises and
the first of which silently discarded most of a stylesheet.

`FindClosingBrace`, `FindTopLevelDelimiter` and `CssSyntax.SplitTopLevel`
tracked strings and comments but not escapes, so the `\}` in `error: \};`
closed the rule it sits in. Everything after it re-parsed one token out of
phase and was dropped -- in Acid2 that was every rule from
`ul { display: table }` on, i.e. the whole last line of the face. CSS Syntax
S4.3.7 says a `\` not followed by a newline escapes the next code point, so
the three scanners now skip it.

A stray top-level `;` then abandoned the rest of the sheet outright. Per
CSS Syntax S5.4.2 a `;` is not a prelude terminator: it makes the *next*
rule's prelude an invalid selector list, so that one rule is dropped and
parsing resumes after its block.

A declaration still holding a top-level `!` once `!important` has been taken
off is malformed (CSS2.1 S4.1.9) and is now dropped, so
`border: 5em solid red ! error` no longer paints a border.

Two value-level rules the same section tests, both in the cascade engine. A
`background` layer takes at most one <color>, so `background: red pink`
yields to the earlier `background: yellow`. And outside quirks mode a
non-zero length may not omit its unit, so `width: 200` yields to `width: 2em`
instead of stretching the face's bottom line to nearly three times its width;
the quirks flag reaches the cascade through the new thread-static
`CssDocumentMode`, which Broiler.HTML publishes on each parse (Broiler.CSS
cannot reference the flag's home in Broiler.Layout -- the dependency runs the
other way).

Border shorthands now reset the longhands they omit and take part in
cascade-time longhand seeding, so `border: solid 1em black; border-top: 0`
erases the top border instead of keeping it. Acid2's nose is written that way
and the leftover 1em black edge drew a bar straight across the face.
